{"tool_name":"lra","contents":["biocontainers","oeb","bioschemas","biotools"],"fetched_metadata":{"biocontainers":{"name":"lra","identifiers":["doi:10.1101/2020.11.15.383273"],"license":"USC-RL v1.0","summary":"Long read aligner for sequences and contigs","home_url":"https://github.com/ChaissonLab/LRA","keywords":["Clustering","Sequence Alignment"],"manually_check":true,"total_pulls":893},"biotools":{"id":"lra","home":"https://anaconda.org/bioconda/lra","summary":"the Long Read Aligner for Sequences and Contigs.\n\nLRA, the long read aligner for sequences and assembly contigs LRA is a sequence alignment program that aligns long reads from single-molecule sequencing (SMS) instruments, or megabase-scale contigs from SMS assemblies. LRA implements seed chaining sparse dynamic programming with a convex gap function to read and assembly alignment, which is also extended to allow for inversion cases. Through the Truvari analysis of LRA, Minimap2 and NGM-LR alignments. LRA achieves higher f1 score over HG002 HiFi, CLR and ONT datasets.\n\nHome: https://github.com/ChaissonLab/LRA.\n\nLong read aligner for sequences and contigs.","addition_date":"2021-01-18T11:45:50Z","last_update_date":"2021-02-19T08:01:54Z","tool_type":["Library"],"biotools_curie":"biotools:lra","credit":[{"email":"mchaisso@usc.edu","name":"Mark JP Chaisson","typeEntity":"Person"}],"edit_permission":{"type":"private"},"function":[{"operation":[{"term":"Genome indexing","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_3211"},{"term":"Read mapping","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_3198"},{"term":"Sequence alignment","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_0292"},{"term":"Sequence assembly","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_0310"},{"term":"Variant calling","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_3227"}]}],"name":"lra","owner":"Niclaskn","publication":[{"doi":"10.1101/2020.11.15.383273"}],"topic":[{"term":"Bioinformatics","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_0091"},{"term":"Sequence assembly","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_0196"},{"term":"Structure analysis","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_0081"},{"term":"Whole genome sequencing","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_3673"}]},"bioschemas":{"name":"lra","home":"https://bio.tools/lra","summary":"the Long Read Aligner for Sequences and Contigs.\n\nLRA, the long read aligner for sequences and assembly contigs LRA is a sequence alignment program that aligns long reads from single-molecule sequencing (SMS) instruments, or megabase-scale contigs from SMS assemblies. LRA implements seed chaining sparse dynamic programming with a convex gap function to read and assembly alignment, which is also extended to allow for inversion cases. Through the Truvari analysis of LRA, Minimap2 and NGM-LR alignments. LRA achieves higher f1 score over HG002 HiFi, CLR and ONT datasets.\n\nHome: https://github.com/ChaissonLab/LRA.\n\nLong read aligner for sequences and contigs.","tool_type":"sc:SoftwareApplication"},"oeb":{"metrics":[{"@id":"https://openebench.bsc.es/monitor/metrics/biotools:lra/lib/anaconda.org","@license":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/","@nmsp":"biotools","@type":"metrics","deprecated":true,"distribution":{"sourcecode":{"interpreted":false,"repository":{}}},"project":{"build":{},"deployment":{},"publications":[{"entries":[{"cit_count":0,"citations":[],"doi":"10.1101/2020.11.15.383273","ref_count":0,"refs":[]}]}],"summary":{"description":true},"website":{"bioschemas":false,"copyright":false,"https":true,"license":false,"operational":200,"ssl":true,"ssl_err":null}}},{"@id":"https://openebench.bsc.es/monitor/metrics/bioconda:lra:1.3.7.2/cmd/github.com","@license":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/","@nmsp":"bioconda","@type":"metrics","distribution":{"packages":true,"sourcecode":{}},"project":{"build":{},"deployment":{},"license":{"open_source":false,"osi":false},"publications":[],"summary":{"description":true},"website":{"bioschemas":true,"copyright":false,"https":true,"license":false,"op